# No long dashes in site copy

Never use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) in any user-facing website text.

Applies to:

- Project descriptions, SEO blurbs, and titles in `content/`
- About, intro, experience, education, and contact copy
- UI strings, metadata titles, form messages, and empty-state placeholders
- Any new copy written for this portfolio

Use instead:

- A comma, period, colon, or parentheses for a pause
- A regular hyphen (`-`) for compound words and date ranges (`2021 - Present`)
- A spaced hyphen (` - `) only when a title already uses that pattern

Do not:

- Convert `" - "` to `" — "` in components or utilities
- Insert typographic long dashes for “polish”

When editing existing copy, replace any `—` or `–` you find.
